ltrspace-prestrain.out
Prestrained tetrahedron against the same deformation of its original configuration
StaticStructural nsteps 2 deltat 1.0 rtolv 1.e-11 maxiter 20 manrmsteps 1 nmodules 1
errorcheck
domain 3d
OutputManager tstep_all dofman_all element_all
ndofman 8 nelem 2 ncrosssect 1 nmat 1 nbc 8 nic 0 nltf 1 nset 8
# Element 1 is the tetrahedron of the mesh (nodes 1-4) with the prestrain f0 = F0 from its original,
# stress-free configuration (F0 has shear, is not symmetric, det F0 = 1.07025). Element 2 (nodes 5-8) is that
# original configuration, X0 = F0^-1 X, without prestrain. Both are moved to the same current positions
# x = G X, so the material sees F = G F0 in both, and the nodal forces of element 1,
# V_X P F0^T / det F0 grad_X N, equal those of element 2, V_X0 P grad_X0 N. Node 4 is free and loaded by
# the reaction of node 8, so it has to end at x4 = G X4 (u4 = 0, 0.05, 0.03), and nodes 1-3 have the
# reactions of nodes 5-7. A transposed or wrongly rotated F0 changes both.
node 1 coords 3 0 0 0
node 2 coords 3 1 0 0
node 3 coords 3 0 1 0
node 4 coords 3 0 0 1
node 5 coords 3 0 0 0
node 6 coords 3 0.91800981079187105 -0.049053959355290826 0.0070077084793272607
node 7 coords 3 -0.19621583742116327 1.079187105816398 -0.15416958654519972
node 8 coords 3 0.018687222611539361 -0.10277972436346648 0.96706377014716183
ltrspace 1 nodes 4 1 2 3 4 crossSect 1 mat 1 nlgeo 1 prestrain 1 f0 9 1.1000000000000001 0.94999999999999996 1.05 0.10000000000000001 0 0.20000000000000001 0.14999999999999999 0 0.050000000000000003
ltrspace 2 nodes 4 5 6 7 8 crossSect 1 mat 1 nlgeo 1
SimpleCS 1 thick 1.0
BlatzKoMat 1 mu 1. d 0.
BoundaryCondition 1 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 3 1 2 3 values 3 0 0 0 set 1
BoundaryCondition 2 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 3 1 2 3 values 3 0.050000000000000044 0 0.02 set 2
BoundaryCondition 3 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 3 1 2 3 values 3 0.10000000000000001 -0.020000000000000018 0 set 3
NodalLoad 4 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 3 1 2 3 components 3 -4.6178516188e-03 4.8483374927e-02 3.2521408373e-02 set 4
BoundaryCondition 5 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 3 1 2 3 values 3 0 0 0 set 5
BoundaryCondition 6 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 3 1 2 3 values 3 0.13199018920812899 0.049053959355290826 0.012992291520672741 set 6
BoundaryCondition 7 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 3 1 2 3 values 3 0.29621583742116331 -0.099187105816398002 0.15416958654519972 set 7
BoundaryCondition 8 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 3 1 2 3 values 3 -0.018687222611539361 0.15277972436346648 0.062936229852838199 set 8
PiecewiseLinFunction 1 npoints 2 t 2 0 2 f(t) 2 0 1
Set 1 nodes 1 1
Set 2 nodes 1 2
Set 3 nodes 1 3
Set 4 nodes 1 4
Set 5 nodes 1 5
Set 6 nodes 1 6
Set 7 nodes 1 7
Set 8 nodes 1 8
#%BEGIN_CHECK% tolerance 1.e-9
